EIGHTY — CS-80 x Jupiter-8 synth plugin
Version: __VERSION__  (built __DATE__ from __REF__)
Apple Silicon Macs only (M1 / M2 / M3 / M4). Won't run on an Intel Mac.

WHAT'S IN THIS FOLDER
  Eighty.vst3        - VST3 plugin (Ableton, Cubase, Studio One, Reaper, etc.)
  Eighty.component   - Audio Unit / AU plugin (Logic Pro, GarageBand, MainStage)
  Install.command     - double-click to install both automatically

────────────────────────────────────────
EASY INSTALL (recommended)
────────────────────────────────────────
1. Double-click "Install.command".
2. macOS will likely refuse to run it the first time and say it's from an
   unidentified developer. If so:
     - Right-click (or Control-click) "Install.command" -> choose "Open"
     - Click "Open" again in the dialog that appears
   This is a one-time step for the installer script itself.
3. A Terminal window will open, copy the plugins into place, and print
   "Done." Press Return to close it.
4. Restart your DAW (or use its "rescan plugins" option) and look for
   "Eighty" under both VST3 and Audio Unit instruments.

────────────────────────────────────────
MANUAL INSTALL (if you'd rather not run the script)
────────────────────────────────────────
1. Copy Eighty.vst3 to:       ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/
2. Copy Eighty.component to:  ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/
   (In Finder: Go menu -> Go to Folder... -> paste the path above)
3. Open Terminal and run these two commands so Gatekeeper doesn't block
   the plugin (it's signed ad-hoc, not through the Mac App Store or a
   paid Apple Developer ID, so macOS is extra cautious about it):
       xattr -cr ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/Eighty.vst3
       xattr -cr ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Eighty.component
4. Restart your DAW and rescan plugins.

────────────────────────────────────────
WHAT'S NEW
────────────────────────────────────────
See the release notes on GitHub for what changed in this build:
  https://github.com/aar75/Eighty/releases

────────────────────────────────────────
TROUBLESHOOTING
────────────────────────────────────────
"Eighty is damaged and can't be opened" / plugin doesn't show up in your DAW:
  - Almost always means the quarantine flag wasn't cleared. Re-run step 3
    of the manual install (the two `xattr -cr` commands) and rescan.

Logic Pro / MainStage still doesn't see it:
  - Open Terminal and run:  auval -v aumu Ei80 ArjR
    This validates the AU directly and will show any error in detail.

Presets and settings from a previous version are kept - they live in
~/Library/Eighty/ and are not touched by installing.

Issues and questions: https://github.com/aar75/Eighty/issues
